{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099352-clan-banes","id":1099352,"title":"Clan banes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-01T18:46:58-07:00","id":1099352,"title":"Clan banes","content":"I was recently reading the 2nd edition of Requiem. I liked the new mechanics for Humanity - focusing more on characters being &quot;not human&quot; rather than &quot;monsters&quot;. Reading your own obituary, surviving a car crash unscathed, joining a covenant, etc. - all make sense. It's nice that characters don't risk getting some derangement whenever they lose humanity - this balances the system so that each humanity lost is noticeable, but not crippling to the character. All good!<br /> <br /> But then I read further into the Clan Banes and they seem to be all over the place. Hit Humanity 6 once and you're in for a permanent problem. But even then those aren't all that balanced.<br /> <br /> Daeva - get addicted to people. Thematic, interesting, encourages having some dots in Herd.<br /> Gangrel - easier frenzy. Okay, harsh, but not that damaging when you recover humanity.<br /> Venture - easier to lose Touchstone. Okay, so in other words, put a dot in the Touchstone merit and you're sort of normal? Gain humanity back and you can fill that slot back in perhaps? Doesn't sound that bad.<br /> <br /> And the fun ones.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu - basically a permanent -1 or more when dealing with mortals? Dramatic failures by default? Okay, that's a bit harsh. In 1st edition they were a bit more &quot;socially awkward&quot; characters, but with this they will have some hard time dealing with people.<br /> Mekhet - get a permanent bane. Okay, so once you hit Humanity 6, you get to act like a b-movie vampire, plus you get one less die on retaining your humanity?<br /> <br /> So a Daeva gets a bit obsessed with a person, while a Nosferatu gets a permanent hit to his social rolls with humans. A Venture gets to spend 1XP to mitigate his problem, while a Mekhet now looks like a corpse with glowing red eyes when he gets peckish? Eesh.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition Requiem had a good idea moving away from the forced derangement, but the Clan Banes are going back into that territory. Worse even - in the 1st edition the derangement would pass if you regained humanity, while those Banes persist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12211-thepiachu","name":"ThePiachu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T18:58:12-07:00","id":1099355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThePiachu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099352-clan-banes#post1099352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mekhet - get a permanent bane. Okay, so once you hit Humanity 6, you get to act like a b-movie vampire, plus you get one less die on retaining your humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a minor correction: The extra bane doesn't add any penalty to detachment checks.<br /> <br /> Other than that I could point out that low Humanity Ventrue will have a harder time holding on to their Humanity since the Touchstone Merit is limited to five dots. At Humanity 2 they can have a single attached Touchstone while the other clans can have two. At Humanity 1 they can't have any attached Touchstone at all.<br /> And even when your Ventrue character doesn't have such low Humanity you still have one additional Touchstone for roleplaying purposes compared to vampires of the same Humanity level.<br /> That said I do think that high to medium Humanity Ventrues by far has the best clan bane. It's mostly just an issue when at Humanity 2-1. I just wanted to point it out since you seemed to have missed the extra risk at low Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:39:24-07:00","id":1099368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099352-clan-banes?p=1099355#post1099355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than that I could point out that low Humanity Ventrue will have a harder time holding on to their Humanity since the Touchstone Merit is limited to five dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, low-low humanity will be an issue, but by then you'll have a Gangrel that goes into Frenzy often, a Nosferatu that fails all social rolls with humans, and a Mekhet that gets 10 levels od damage when they hear bells or is reduced to a cripple by someone wielding a cross.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Venture will be much easier reduced to Humanity 0 once they reach ~Humanity 2.<br /> <br /> I guess Daevas are the ones that are the most consistent through their Humanity - &quot;I like this mortal, I like them a lot&quot; for both Humanity 6 and Humanity 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12211-thepiachu","name":"ThePiachu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:46:50-07:00","id":1099370,"title":"","content":"Then again, I can't really imagine Daeva being that functional long-term once they get their Bane, unless I'm missing something from the rules.<br /> <br /> Once you drink a second time from a mortal, you get a level 2 blood bond with them essentially. If there is no time limit on that, you will eventually make bonds with your entire herd. 100 people? That's about a year's worth of feeding. Then either you have a handful of your favourite blood bags to drink from, or a whole village of people you have strong emotional bonds with. At that point you probably risk constant Detachment from the antisocial behaviours, or take a Bane and try figuring out how to have a shred of sanity in your life...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12211-thepiachu","name":"ThePiachu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T20:45:44-07:00","id":1099380,"title":"","content":"Does the Daeva bane create permanent obsessions, though? I heard that even the Vinculum, at less-than-maximum levels, can fade given enough time.<br /> <br /> For the Ventrue bane, a homebrew that came up in the past that I thought was nice was limiting the Willpower gain you normally get from interacting with your Touchstones. In situations where other vampires would automatically regain 1 Willpower from interacting with them, the Ventrue need to roll Humanity and succeed. And where other vampires would regain full Willpower, the Ventrue rolls Humanity and only gets Willpower equal to successes. Can't remember whose idea this was, though.<br /> <br /> Another one of the past comments on the Ventrue bane was that it's less about mechanics and more about narratives. Even jaded vampires who care little for others love and care for their Touchstones. But the Ventrue have a hard time relating to even their most precious ones. Then how would the Ventrue treat others who are not even Touchstones at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T02:05:46-07:00","id":1099416,"title":"","content":"That one was mine. <br /> <br /> I also reworked the Gangrel's so you get penalties to Frenzy rolls similar to the ones you get for social interaction instead of a cap, as I found caps don't work that well. <br /> <br /> Nosferatu's focus on Social Maneuvering, reducing average First Impression if your Humanity is lower than the Integrity equivalent of the other party and adding extra Doors based on the difference. This doesn't apply in the case of Intimidation, Hard Leverage or Forcing Doors. <br /> <br /> Last I make Mekhet in my canon to be closer to death, so they need to pay extra Vitae to use the Blush of Life* or they look like obvious animated corpses. <br /> <br /> *Half the inverse of Humanity rounded up, so 1 extra Vitae at Humanity 10-9, 2 extra at Humanity 8-7, and so on, up to 5 extra at Humanity 1-2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T10:30:19-07:00","id":1099565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThePiachu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099352-clan-banes#post1099352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daeva - get addicted to people. Thematic, interesting, encourages having some dots in Herd.<br /> Gangrel - easier frenzy. Okay, harsh, but not that damaging when you recover humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice that frenzy now comes with a drive behind them, picked by the situation at hand, or the player. It could be as harsh as wanting to humilliate someone, throw some mean spirited insults and force the victim to leave the premises under the weight of the psychological assault and you'd be done with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThePiachu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099352-clan-banes#post1099352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Venture - easier to lose Touchstone. Okay, so in other words, put a dot in the Touchstone merit and you're sort of normal? Gain humanity back and you can fill that slot back in perhaps? Doesn't sound that bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically speaking it's the system way to emulate the adage &quot;it's lonely at the top.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThePiachu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099352-clan-banes#post1099352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the fun ones.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu - basically a permanent -1 or more when dealing with mortals? Dramatic failures by default? Okay, that's a bit harsh. In 1st edition they were a bit more &quot;socially awkward&quot; characters, but with this they will have some hard time dealing with people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice that Touchstones are exempt. Even Nosferatu can find reliance in say, a True Friend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThePiachu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099352-clan-banes#post1099352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mekhet - get a permanent bane. Okay, so once you hit Humanity 6, you get to act like a b-movie vampire, plus you get one less die on retaining your humanity?<br /> <br /> So a Daeva gets a bit obsessed with a person, while a Nosferatu gets a permanent hit to his social rolls with humans. A Venture gets to spend 1XP to mitigate his problem, while a Mekhet now looks like a corpse with glowing red eyes when he gets peckish? Eesh.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition Requiem had a good idea moving away from the forced derangement, but the Clan Banes are going back into that territory. Worse even - in the 1st edition the derangement would pass if you regained humanity, while those Banes persist...</div> </div> </div> </div>Clan Banes are the tip of the iceberg. Slip further, something that's very likely to happen, and you'll get your own, custom banes. The familiarity in the clan banes comes from a need to relay parentage, which is what clans are. Bloodlines.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T14:57:08-07:00","id":1100225,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing about the Ventrue bane: you can definitely buy a one dot Merit to account for it and forget about it. Wham bam thank you ma'am.<br /> <br /> <i>But, </i>if you were playing at my table, just for example, I'd ask you to work for that relationship. It's a Touchstone. It's the core of your Humanity. If the player is treating a new Touchstone as a get out of jail free card (and if they think of banes as a punishment, then that's a problem in and of itself), then they're missing the point of the mechanic. The idea behind the Ventrue bane is to get the player into interesting situations...or to revel in sociopathy (as the case may be). It's not a tax, it's a plot hook.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, I've been in a game for the last half year where the Nosferatu Bane hasn't come up once, compared to a Requiem game I ran where the Ventrue bane came up almost every session.<br /> <br /> Which, that being said, can matter less if your game isn't that focused on Touchstones. But banes aren't really intended to come up at an equally distributed rate of play. I've literally never seen the Gangrel bane come up, for example, but I still think it's a pretty good one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T08:39:06-07:00","id":1100857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1099352-clan-banes?p=1099416#post1099416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That one was mine.<br /> <br /> I also reworked the Gangrel's so you get penalties to Frenzy rolls similar to the ones you get for social interaction instead of a cap, as I found caps don't work that well.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu's focus on Social Maneuvering, reducing average First Impression if your Humanity is lower than the Integrity equivalent of the other party and adding extra Doors based on the difference. This doesn't apply in the case of Intimidation, Hard Leverage or Forcing Doors.<br /> <br /> Last I make Mekhet in my canon to be closer to death, so they need to pay extra Vitae to use the Blush of Life* or they look like obvious animated corpses.<br /> <br /> *Half the inverse of Humanity rounded up, so 1 extra Vitae at Humanity 10-9, 2 extra at Humanity 8-7, and so on, up to 5 extra at Humanity 1-2</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thorbes, these are very interesting. I assume you've summarized. Do you have a full post describing your tweaks?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T14:16:38-07:00","id":1100960,"title":"","content":"Besides a little flavour text and personal notes of why this work for me (for example, Nosferatu benefit of dealing with very broken people, even dragging them to their level with Nightmare) that's pretty much it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}